# Customer Churn Analysis

## Project Overview

Customer churn refers to customers who stop using a service or cancel their subscriptions. This project analyzes customer behavior data to identify factors that contribute to churn and provides recommendations to improve customer retention.

---

## Objectives

- Analyze customer activity and engagement.
- Measure churn rate.
- Identify behavioral patterns of churned customers.
- Generate actionable retention recommendations.

---

## Dataset Features

| Column | Description |
|----------|------------|
| CustomerID | Unique customer identifier |
| Age | Customer age |
| SubscriptionMonths | Length of subscription |
| LoginFrequency | Number of logins per month |
| SupportTickets | Customer support requests |
| MonthlyCharges | Monthly subscription fee |
| Churn | Whether customer left the service |

---

## Technologies Used

- Python
- Pandas

---

## Project Structure

```text
customer-churn-analysis/
│
├── churn_analysis.py
├── customer_data.csv
├── churn_report.csv
├── requirements.txt
└── README.md
```

---

## Installation

```bash
git clone https://github.com/your-username/customer-churn-analysis.git
cd customer-churn-analysis
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

---

## Run Project

```bash
python churn_analysis.py
```

---

## Sample Insights

The analysis evaluates:

- Churn Rate
- User Login Frequency
- Support Ticket Activity
- Customer Engagement Trends

---

## Retention Strategies

- Personalized promotions for inactive users
- Faster support response times
- Loyalty programs for long-term subscribers
- Engagement campaigns for low-activity customers

---

## Output

A report file:

```text
churn_report.csv
```

containing summarized churn metrics and findings.

---

## Learning Outcomes

- Customer behavior analysis
- Business intelligence reporting
- Churn prediction concepts
- Data-driven decision making

